{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"a34f6351d13f67c45d3b0ba48b3ac3d17b1e39885966818fa2315a362b8e4afa","digest":{"component_or_area":"mcp service docker-compose configuration","key_entities":["infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL","REBAR_MCP_AUTH_RESOURCE_SERVER_URL","src/rebar/mcp_server.py","AuthSettings","fetch-secrets.sh","tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_auth.py"],"problem_keywords":["environment variable missing","docker-compose configuration","crash-loop","pydantic validation","fresh deploy","auth settings"],"propositions":["The mcp service in docker-compose.yml omits the REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL environment variable.","AuthSettings pydantic model raises ValidationError on container startup because issuer_url is empty, causing crash-loop.","The compose environment block sets REBAR_MCP_AUTH_RESOURCE_SERVER_URL but not its sibling REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL, creating an asymmetry.","The /health endpoint never comes up on fresh deploy due to auth settings construction failure.","Unit tests in test_mcp_auth.py always set auth_issuer_url explicitly, so the compose omission gap was not caught."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787719093617869001,"uuid":"69f0badd-cb82-41dd-8349-cf3e8f6f83de"}